<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="Hawker Range Systems Ltd" id="id-372bb0b5443c4ad68a1630904c51e539" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-0b3f7ca277cb49de952365dd03f88529" type="strategy">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Task" id="id-637e89c75e944169983f389d7a572f98">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-02-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-02
Capability that covers sortie tasking on the path into the range day. Planning-facing ownership stays with RangePlan; this is not live GCS and not an application element.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Clear" id="id-97ebdecf31914a67bb2dbd87f3229ddb">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-02-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-02
Capability that covers clearance before a sortie is handed to live control. Sits between tasking and live GCS on the tasking-to-live-sortie path.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Fly" id="id-03db6547aef1422db55f7e1277e94923">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-02-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-02
Capability that covers the live sortie under GCS control. GroundOS owns live-sortie for this capability in documentation only; AirStack remains the airborne path and is not replaced here. No application elements on this view.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Recover" id="id-44a1e398965248e8a79831ea7cc78298">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-02-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-02
Capability that covers recover after the live sortie segment. Closes the tasking-to-live-sortie map after Fly; does not expand into nodes, processes, or work packages.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-5643e0ababcc4ce28c2991ac5d7a7a4d" type="business">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Task" id="id-8b426a10197b48b4b0864f0b4445ec3e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
As-is range-floor process that opens the sortie day with a tasked identity. Distinct from the Task capability; SortieBoard remains the pain, not a drawn application.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Clear" id="id-c0d2f85265bb4414b03c5a7e69934983">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
As-is clearance handoff before live control takes the sortie. Distinct from the Clear capability; no application component created for this step.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Fly" id="id-b866710ad3b448d3829e71df6397738f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
As-is live GCS control period for the sortie on the range floor. Distinct from the Fly capability; GroundOS stays documentation-only this job.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Recover" id="id-43ccf54a35034dfe8b7846c141d8f6b5">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
As-is recover step that closes the live period after fly. Distinct from the Recover capability; no air-vehicle structure and no nodes this job.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Range Manager" id="id-20972da34bbb434ab4ffe45eed56b121">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Business role that runs clearance on the range floor for the as-is chain. Motivation stakeholder of the same name is reused off this type; not duplicated as Stakeholder.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Chief Instructor" id="id-d43bcfe1df2448359ea677c9b5135051">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Business role that closes recover on the instructor side of the range day. Motivation stakeholder of the same name stays the job-1 ID; this is the assignment role only.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Sortie Planner" id="id-9e06116e788e40239a3ad697c91a2d06">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Business role that performs tasking into the range day. SortieBoard is still the pain in narrative; no new planning application is introduced here.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="GCS Owner" id="id-b25651dc1b5e44399395fbce5ba90087">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Business role that owns the live fly period under GCS control language. No GroundOS rewrite and no application component on this view.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Application" id="id-79e77e92bf7243d18858bb5ae6760621" type="application">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="AirStack" id="id-4c7eefcd80b44e7586295bded35cddb5">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
Airborne mission computer application for the live sortie. Stays separate from RangePlan and GroundOS; not planning software and not the GCS.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="GroundOS" id="id-a3eaf0c0d5b74284a190ac0c70c4830d">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
Ground control station software that owns the live sortie on the range floor. Must not be swallowed by RangePlan; remains the live-control application.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="SortieBoard" id="id-e163a120914643a5904ce0d5bcdc1fa6">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
As-is shared-drive spreadsheet of the day's sorties; the known pain system. Modelled as an ApplicationComponent so the five named systems stay visible.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="RangePlan" id="id-1f24a5f8fd8846df99eccfc2157a1663">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
Mission-planning tool in pilot, funded for sortie visibility only. Stays planning-facing and separate from AirStack and GroundOS; not drawn as the GCS.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="LinkGate" id="id-23d0ad9fc6be4d2b93b3fabd9f6ca0c9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
Ground datalink gateway application that bridges RangePlan tasking into GroundOS. Does not talk to the air vehicle; no equipment or air-vehicle interface this job.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Technology &amp; Physical" id="id-4cea9c75a1d84ac9b636f84e77887d70" type="technology">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Range floor node" id="id-38c34403663d47f89cb62a7240e16e5f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Range-floor compute and control locus for launch kit on the range pad. Hosts Launch equipment assignment; does not host RangePlan or AirStack.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="On-prem app server" id="id-996182b6c7394a038accf601f3139a0a">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
On-premises application server that hosts GroundOS for live GCS control. RangePlan is deliberately not placed here.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="LinkGate node" id="id-0c90872c58974113baf4ef07d05bf59e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Node inside the comms cabin that hosts the LinkGate gateway application. Separate from the range floor and from any air-vehicle interface.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Facility" name="Hangar" id="id-54ebbe9850ae4485b5932078a0c8cc14">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Range hangar facility at Moorfield Range. Physical shelter context only; not an application host and not air-vehicle product structure.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Facility" name="GCS van" id="id-7b2d4974798e4faeabed3599b8ae08f2">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Ground control station van as a facility location on the range site. Shelter/location only; GroundOS remains the live-control application, not this van.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Facility" name="Comms cabin" id="id-622e47e2c1ae42438c8c5fe4b2929cff">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Communications cabin housing the LinkGate host node and datalink path. Keeps gateway infrastructure off the range floor and off any air-vehicle draw.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Equipment" name="Datalink mast" id="id-024345e85bea4028bb2e35bf46be6752">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Ground datalink mast equipment near the cabin path. Supports ground links; LinkGate still does not talk to the air vehicle.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Equipment" name="Launch equipment" id="id-f2e4e924c5ed4ff09eb64fffd09551f1">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Launch equipment on the range floor. Assigned to the range-floor node so physical kit is visible and distinct from planning software.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Motivation" id="id-1b22b99f46804205b5746e19133735f3" type="motivation">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Range Manager" id="id-f1cf33210db04f8d80c4d357b35eeede">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Owns the morning on-range answer for range control. Signs the Motivation Overview with the Chief Instructor.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Chief Instructor" id="id-bc23506291674caf8f55964f0381568b">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Owns the same morning on-range answer for instructors. Needs SortieBoard dual tracking to stop.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="GCS Owner" id="id-37db77111a96462299c6f4f7a06c2079">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Keeps GroundOS as the live GCS system of record. Boundary witness that RangePlan is not a GroundOS replacement.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Planning Programme Manager" id="id-5eee5b3ec1074f10a684417d23c4242b">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Holds RangePlan to planning-facing visibility scope. Funds the fix without expanding into GroundOS or AirStack rewrite.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Sortie Planner" id="id-ff2c9308cb134f2e98350b6087097981">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Needs one sortie identity from tasking through live GCS so planned and flown days stop diverging.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Integration Lead" id="id-7a10b06f1bfa41e5b30885ee93d65d7c">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Carries shared identity across systems without merging GroundOS or AirStack into RangePlan.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Driver" name="Promised sortie times do not match what the range can fly" id="id-407b7250961f4e029b285f64965e37cd">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
External and internal promises outrun what Moorfield Range can actually fly on the day. Creates dual tracking and loss of a single morning answer.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Goal" name="Instructors and the range share one sortie identity from tasking to live GCS" id="id-d262b5beaf4a46a9bf3a03a1a7f6a319">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Desired state is one shared sortie identity from tasking into the live GCS path. Not a merged system blob.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Outcome" name="Range Manager and Chief Instructor answer on-range-this-morning without SortieBoard" id="id-00c2c5228d494559b21c5c10f8f53359">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Signatories can answer whether a sortie is on the range this morning without consulting the shared-drive spreadsheet.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="RangePlan must not swallow AirStack or GroundOS" id="id-ec762c52e806466fa6eded750caa15e0">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Hard freeze: RangePlan stays planning-facing. AirStack remains the airborne mission computer and GroundOS remains the live GCS. Named systems appear in this text only; they are not application elements on this view.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Implementation &amp; Migration" id="id-c916e6d1624a45ff8a40fd46fe75e353" type="implementation_migration"/>
  <folder name="Other" id="id-9d5c381e0c2846bc892ea266673fd102" type="other"/>
