Sortie Planner is concerned with the mismatch between promised and flyable sortie times at Moorfield Range.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssociationRelationship" id="id-d88be420fd5e4298a99c06f64033a495" source="id-7a10b06f1bfa41e5b30885ee93d65d7c" target="id-407b7250961f4e029b285f64965e37cd">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Integration Lead is concerned with the mismatch between promised and flyable sortie times at Moorfield Range.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:InfluenceRelationship" id="id-399c8f100a054f4dac0ff089cc3f477d" source="id-407b7250961f4e029b285f64965e37cd" target="id-d262b5beaf4a46a9bf3a03a1a7f6a319">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
The mismatch drives the need for one shared sortie identity from tasking to live GCS.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:RealizationRelationship" id="id-03ec9a4d2ea240abbf44d77d1622016d" source="id-ec762c52e806466fa6eded750caa15e0" target="id-d262b5beaf4a46a9bf3a03a1a7f6a319">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Shared identity is achieved without collapsing RangePlan, AirStack, and GroundOS into one system.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:InfluenceRelationship" id="id-815b5d3ce08c42b48927569b39c85469" source="id-d262b5beaf4a46a9bf3a03a1a7f6a319" target="id-00c2c5228d494559b21c5c10f8f53359">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-01-view-plan.md
Shared sortie identity yields the morning on-range answer without SortieBoard.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-9859c332fee245449a2e73c86679c868" source="id-9e06116e788e40239a3ad697c91a2d06" target="id-8b426a10197b48b4b0864f0b4445ec3e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Sortie Planner is assigned to the Task process on the as-is range floor chain. Assignment is business-layer only; SortieBoard stays the pain in documentation.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-cb4300984071419c87c1a537c0148ab0" source="id-20972da34bbb434ab4ffe45eed56b121" target="id-c0d2f85265bb4414b03c5a7e69934983">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Range Manager is assigned to the Clear process on the as-is range floor chain. Assignment is business-layer only; SortieBoard stays the pain in documentation.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-e4108767c6d9403eb038b4ad98f44673" source="id-b25651dc1b5e44399395fbce5ba90087" target="id-b866710ad3b448d3829e71df6397738f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
GCS Owner is assigned to the Fly process on the as-is range floor chain. Assignment is business-layer only; SortieBoard stays the pain in documentation.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-fb87b731bffb455198412a99e5b67f62" source="id-d43bcfe1df2448359ea677c9b5135051" target="id-43ccf54a35034dfe8b7846c141d8f6b5">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Chief Instructor is assigned to the Recover process on the as-is range floor chain. Assignment is business-layer only; SortieBoard stays the pain in documentation.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TriggeringRelationship" id="id-e695269512f9459d9f003d84ff7c5eec" source="id-8b426a10197b48b4b0864f0b4445ec3e" target="id-c0d2f85265bb4414b03c5a7e69934983">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Task triggers Clear on the as-is task-clear-fly-recover handoff. No application, node, or air-vehicle structure is introduced by this edge.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TriggeringRelationship" id="id-b4680b8852914b9088c737e220bf140c" source="id-c0d2f85265bb4414b03c5a7e69934983" target="id-b866710ad3b448d3829e71df6397738f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Clear triggers Fly on the as-is task-clear-fly-recover handoff. No application, node, or air-vehicle structure is introduced by this edge.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TriggeringRelationship" id="id-0bb0bba503c84905a1f0351f84806fac" source="id-b866710ad3b448d3829e71df6397738f" target="id-43ccf54a35034dfe8b7846c141d8f6b5">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-03-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-03
Fly triggers Recover on the as-is task-clear-fly-recover handoff. No application, node, or air-vehicle structure is introduced by this edge.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-35f0a22b97954c5580aa2cbb88fb3684" source="id-1f24a5f8fd8846df99eccfc2157a1663" target="id-8b426a10197b48b4b0864f0b4445ec3e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
RangePlan serves the reused Task process (planning tool supports tasking). Light cross-layer edge only; does not redraw Range Operations or merge apps.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-592259ddd4314163b65dc39eb9bc8c45" source="id-e163a120914643a5904ce0d5bcdc1fa6" target="id-8b426a10197b48b4b0864f0b4445ec3e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
SortieBoard serves the reused Task process (as-is spreadsheet still used at tasking). Light cross-layer edge only; does not redraw Range Operations or merge apps.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-a92d87c3d13c4055b3f0a1ca62adec28" source="id-23d0ad9fc6be4d2b93b3fabd9f6ca0c9" target="id-c0d2f85265bb4414b03c5a7e69934983">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
LinkGate serves the reused Clear process (bridge supports clearance handoff into live). Light cross-layer edge only; does not redraw Range Operations or merge apps.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-92a6612843ba4b4594034a1a1a07e4ed" source="id-a3eaf0c0d5b74284a190ac0c70c4830d" target="id-b866710ad3b448d3829e71df6397738f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
GroundOS serves the reused Fly process (GCS software owns live fly). Light cross-layer edge only; does not redraw Range Operations or merge apps.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-f766d382c6f549efa292c3711c2e97a9" source="id-4c7eefcd80b44e7586295bded35cddb5" target="id-b866710ad3b448d3829e71df6397738f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
AirStack serves the reused Fly process (airborne computer supports the live period). Light cross-layer edge only; does not redraw Range Operations or merge apps.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-23b4391780d54366ae3877e20ec024a4" source="id-a3eaf0c0d5b74284a190ac0c70c4830d" target="id-43ccf54a35034dfe8b7846c141d8f6b5">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
GroundOS serves the reused Recover process (live-control app still in scope at recover close). Light cross-layer edge only; does not redraw Range Operations or merge apps.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-89f559f9f1f043f3a61172f01ab6e546" source="id-1f24a5f8fd8846df99eccfc2157a1663" target="id-23d0ad9fc6be4d2b93b3fabd9f6ca0c9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
RangePlan serves LinkGate with planning tasking for the bridge into live control. Apps remain separate; shared identity stays on the process chain.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ServingRelationship" id="id-a97ea82ce8ba45c2b1c766d834a96aed" source="id-23d0ad9fc6be4d2b93b3fabd9f6ca0c9" target="id-a3eaf0c0d5b74284a190ac0c70c4830d">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-04-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-04
LinkGate serves GroundOS with bridged tasking only; does not talk to the air vehicle. Apps remain separate; shared identity stays on the process chain.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:RealizationRelationship" id="id-68b896e478c8419dacaac1373f2f2b26" source="id-996182b6c7394a038accf601f3139a0a" target="id-a3eaf0c0d5b74284a190ac0c70c4830d">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
On-prem app server hosts GroundOS (realization host→app; Assignment Node→App rejected by bridge). RangePlan is not hosted on this node.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:RealizationRelationship" id="id-10a3dcbbf6d2496fac1256e761854851" source="id-0c90872c58974113baf4ef07d05bf59e" target="id-23d0ad9fc6be4d2b93b3fabd9f6ca0c9">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
LinkGate node in the comms cabin hosts the LinkGate gateway. LinkGate bridges RangePlan tasking to GroundOS only and does not talk to the air vehicle.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-f451ca647fc7405f8fcc03724164f084" source="id-38c34403663d47f89cb62a7240e16e5f" target="id-f2e4e924c5ed4ff09eb64fffd09551f1">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Range-floor node assigns launch equipment so pad kit is visible and distinct from RangePlan/AirStack/GroundOS.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-e169b9f06efd4128a955fa360449f5cb" source="id-54ebbe9850ae4485b5932078a0c8cc14" target="id-38c34403663d47f89cb62a7240e16e5f">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Hangar assigns the range-floor node as pad context.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-5de585d0805045899c8ee4cb3f4ebda1" source="id-7b2d4974798e4faeabed3599b8ae08f2" target="id-996182b6c7394a038accf601f3139a0a">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
GCS van is the facility location near GroundOS hosting; van is not the GroundOS app.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssignmentRelationship" id="id-39efb8cb9e554c4f814cee7aa2e029b9" source="id-622e47e2c1ae42438c8c5fe4b2929cff" target="id-0c90872c58974113baf4ef07d05bf59e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Comms cabin assigns the LinkGate node, off the range floor.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssociationRelationship" id="id-1c59ff1dc5b34dbf8dbd847b523078a9" source="id-024345e85bea4028bb2e35bf46be6752" target="id-0c90872c58974113baf4ef07d05bf59e">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05
Light adjacency of datalink mast to the LinkGate host node in the cabin path. Not a full network inventory; LinkGate still has no air-vehicle interface.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:AssociationRelationship" id="id-b645383bdf924bb5acd43b825d4c5f73" source="id-ec762c52e806466fa6eded750caa15e0" target="id-996182b6c7394a038accf601f3139a0a">
      <documentation>Evidence: stated - docs/moorfield-brief.md; job-05-view-plan.md (approved); architect answers job-05; whole-model light trace
Requirement binds GroundOS hosting: GroundOS stays on the on-prem app server, not merged into RangePlan; AirStack stays off this canvas.</documentation>
    </element>
