      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-941b3e1f36be441390b0dc232a48118e">
        <bounds x="20" y="1165" width="560" height="81"/>
        <content>Sign-off view for Range Manager and Chief Instructor.
Scope: motivation only. Named systems (AirStack, GroundOS, SortieBoard, RangePlan) appear in requirement text only, not as application elements.
Draft (job-01).</content>
      </child>
      <documentation>## Purpose
Record why Moorfield Range needs shared sortie identity without merging planning and live GCS systems. This view is the signed Motivation Overview for job 01.

## Stakeholders and Concerns
Range Manager and Chief Instructor need a morning on-range answer without SortieBoard. GCS Owner and Planning Programme Manager hold the freeze that RangePlan stays planning-facing. Sortie Planner and Integration Lead need one identity from tasking to live GCS without swallowing AirStack or GroundOS.

## Viewpoint
Standard ArchiMate Motivation viewpoint (`motivation`), overview abstraction. Bands: Stakeholders; Drivers and Assessments; Goals and Outcomes; Requirements and Principles.

## Questions Answered
Why do promised sortie times fail the range day? What desired state replaces dual tracking? What hard freeze keeps RangePlan, AirStack, and GroundOS separate while identity is shared?

## Assumptions
Fact freeze is docs/moorfield-brief.md. Model starts empty for Hawker Range Systems Ltd. Named as-is systems are wording only in this job; no application, process, capability, or node elements.

## Decisions
Spine locked to one Driver, one Goal, one Outcome, one Requirement with plain brief names. All six stakeholder roles shown. Shared sortie identity expressed as Goal/Outcome language, not a merged system.

## Exclusions
Capabilities, business processes, application components, technology/physical nodes, work packages, second site, costing, GroundOS rewrite, weapons system, and air-vehicle product/SysML structure.

## Open Questions
None blocking job 01. Later SOAM jobs reuse these IDs for cross-layer work.
</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="Capability Map" id="id-6967b8a5125d46e1b6ba0edbf9b9539b" connectionRouterType="2" viewpoint="capability_map">
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Group" id="id-6771e5b571404912b762cb2a8bd19b50" name="Tasking to live sortie" fillColor="#F4F4F4">
        <bounds x="40" y="40" width="920" height="200"/>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-a97d37f7155b44c99e1950a0ebbb265a" archimateElement="id-637e89c75e944169983f389d7a572f98">
          <bounds x="30" y="50" width="180" height="80"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-0d2563d2823a43a5b039724faaca6ddc" archimateElement="id-97ebdecf31914a67bb2dbd87f3229ddb">
          <bounds x="250" y="50" width="180" height="80"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-12105dc31f1441b98c58a103e953fc49" archimateElement="id-03db6547aef1422db55f7e1277e94923">
          <bounds x="470" y="50" width="180" height="80"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-23206d59a5c3471d8d7cee8d92352534" archimateElement="id-44a1e398965248e8a79831ea7cc78298">
          <bounds x="690" y="50" width="180" height="80"/>
        </child>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-cf6fe7862d284c59abba93b5e9e4c532">
        <bounds x="40" y="260" width="560" height="111"/>
        <content>Ownership (text only; no applications on this view):
- GroundOS owns live-sortie (Fly)
- AirStack remains airborne
- RangePlan stays planning-facing (Task)
Spatial left-to-right order is the map spine; Cap-Cap edges omitted.</content>
      </child>
      <documentation>## Purpose
Agree which strategy capabilities cover tasking through recover on the Moorfield tasking-to-live-sortie path, with ownership boundaries held in plain language.

## Stakeholders and Concerns
Range Manager and Chief Instructor need one agreed capability map. GCS Owner needs GroundOS kept as live-sortie owner on Fly. Planning Programme Manager needs RangePlan kept planning-facing on Task. Sortie Planner needs stable capability names for later SOAM views without a second motivation spine.

## Viewpoint
Standard ArchiMate Capability Map viewpoint (`capability_map`), overview abstraction. Single group band Tasking to live sortie with spatial left-to-right order Task, Clear, Fly, Recover.

## Questions Answered
Which capabilities run tasking, clearance, live GCS, and recover? Where do GroundOS, AirStack, and RangePlan ownership sit without drawing applications? What names stay fixed for later views?

## Assumptions
Fact freeze is docs/moorfield-brief.md. Job 1 Motivation Overview and IDs remain unchanged. Cap-Cap Flow or Association is omitted after the Hatherley lesson; order on the canvas carries the spine. Named systems appear in documentation and the view note only.

## Decisions
Four top-level capabilities with plain names Task, Clear, Fly, Recover. View title Capability Map. GroundOS owns live-sortie on Fly in text only; AirStack airborne; RangePlan planning-facing. No application, process, node, or work-package elements this job.

## Exclusions
Motivation re-modelling, business processes, application components, technology and physical nodes, work packages, second site, costing, GroundOS rewrite, weapons system, air-vehicle product or SysML structure.

## Open Questions
None blocking job 02. Later SOAM jobs attach operations, applications, and technology to these capability IDs.
</documentation>
    </element>
